.Dd October 6, 2026
.Dt DEHEX 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dehex
.Nd decode hexadecimal values as ASCII
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.ad l
.Nm
reads a space-delimited list of hexadecimal bytes from standard input,
printing for each one an
.Tn ASCII
character of the corresponding code point.
Bytes must fall between
.Sy 00
and
.Sy FF
.Pq 255 ;
values outside this range are truncated to their first byte.
.Nm
continues reading input until a blank line
.Pq or Ev EOF
is encountered.
.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Decode and print the word
.Dq Hello
to standard output:
.Dl Li Nm echo Qo Ar 48 65 6C 6C 6F 2E 0A Qc | Nm
.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dc 1 ,
.Xr hexdump 1 ,
.Xr od 1 ,
.Xr xxd 1
.
